      "title": "Present Simple or Present Continuous? (reminder)",
      "tags": {
        "content": [
          "Present Simple",
          "Present Continuous"
        ],
        "levels": [
          "A1",
          "A2"
        ],
        "skills": [
          "Leitura"
        ]
      },
      "block": {
        "type": "explanation",
        "label": "REMINDER · PRESENT SIMPLE OR PRESENT CONTINUOUS?",
        "html": "<span style=\"background-color: #CFE9EA\"><b>PRESENT SIMPLE</b></span> = habits, routine, facts. <i>every day, usually, always, never, on Mondays</i><br><i>I <b>work</b> from home on Fridays. · She <b>works</b> in a bank.</i><br>⚠️ he / she / it → verb + <b>s</b> · negative: <b>don't / doesn't</b> + verb<br><br><span style=\"background-color: #FFE2B8\"><b>PRESENT CONTINUOUS</b></span> = happening now, or around now. <i>now, right now, at the moment, today, these days, Look!</i><br><i>I <b>am working</b> now. · She <b>is working</b> at the moment.</i><br>⚠️ always <b>am / is / are</b> + verb-<b>ing</b>: ✗ <i>I working</i> ✗ <i>I am work</i>"
      }
    },
